> How do I get a date for today of the form "2024-07-08" in python?
**assistant**:
> To get the current date in the format "YYYY-MM-DD" in Python, you can use the `datetime` module. Here's a simple example:
> 
> ```python
> from datetime import datetime
> 
> # Get today's date
> today = datetime.today()
> 
> # Format the date as "YYYY-MM-DD"
> formatted_date = today.strftime("%Y-%m-%d")
> 
> print(formatted_date)
> ```
> 
> This code uses `strftime` to format the date in the desired "YYYY-MM-DD" format.
